    "updated_at": "2016-12-22T19:26:36Z",
    "body": "OK, now I'm back to thinking \"was\". But in these kind of scenarios probably the best thing to do is to rephrase things so that people get less confused. Maybe we can clean up the surrounding text as well. Assuming I am correct about https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2138#issuecomment-268871703, here is what I am thinking:\r\n\r\n1. If the Document's salvageable state is false, then:\r\n    1. Let _window_ be the Document's Window object.\r\n    1. For each EventSource object _eventSource_ whose relevant global object is equal to _window_, forcibly close _eventSource_.\r\n    1. Empty _window_'s list of active timers.",
